L wrote:
> * Traps in corridors generation is now dependant on dungeon level -
> odds per square are 1 in 75 for DL 1, 1 in 73 for DL 2, and increasing
> as such to a limit of 1 in 21.

It seems to me that traps in corridors would make the game dramatically
harder.  Being able to run from trouble is a huge strategic part of
gameplay.  Moreover, walking through a trap may be unavoidable in the
early game if you need to get by it to get to the down stairs, and
you're opening up a host of instadeath possibilities.  Putting traps in
corridors is quite different from putting them in rooms.  In rooms,
normally you can skirt traps (and careful players search before moving
in at least the early/mid game to avoid them for the most part).



